`POST /.netlify/functions/admin-sellers` was returning 500/Unauthorized despite correct DB state (`public.users.role = 'admin'`, valid JWT). The auth logic had fragile fallbacks that masked the real failure path.

## Changes

### `authenticateAdmin`
- **Token extraction**: log `TOKEN EXISTS` immediately after bearer parse — confirms header reaches the function
- **DB query**: narrowed to `select('role')` + `.maybeSingle()` (was `.single()` which throws on missing row)
- **Admin check**: simplified to `dbUser?.role !== 'admin'` — removed `owner` role alias and `ADMIN_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL` email-bypass fallback, both of which could silently grant or deny access unexpectedly
- **Structured logs**: `AUTH USER ID`, `DB USER ROLE` emitted in sequence to pinpoint exactly where auth fails in production logs

### Handler catch block
- Renamed log to `ADMIN SELLERS ERROR` for grep-friendly tracing

```ts
// Before
const isDbAdmin = role === 'admin' || role === 'owner';
const isEmailAdmin = adminEmail !== '' && email === adminEmail;
if (!isDbAdmin && !isEmailAdmin) return { ok: false, status: 403 };

// After
if (dbUser?.role !== 'admin') return { ok: false, status: 403 };
```

## Summary

Adds `BoardMatcher` to golo: shape and pattern matching on a `Board`, with a candidate-move classifier that names moves as `Pass` / `Take` / `Atari` / `Self-Atari` / `Suicide` / `Fill` / `Connect`, opening-library shapes, point names (`Tengen` / `Hoshi` / `4-4 Point`…), or three new additions (`Crosscut` / `Monkey Jump` / `Cap`). All names are translatable into 6 locales matching `igo-social-flutter` (`en` / `ja` / `ko` / `zh` / `zh_HK` / `zh_TW`).

The matching model and the embedded 58-pattern opening library are inherited from [`@sabaki/boardmatcher`](https://github.com/SabakiHQ/boardmatcher) (MIT, attributed in `LICENSE`); the implementation is a Dart-idiomatic rewrite (Int8 sign-map, bitfield hypotheses, iterative liberty traversal).

Cut from `main`, independent of the scoring/estimator PR (#35).

## API surface

```dart
typedef SignedVertex = ({Vertex vertex, int sign});  // sign ∈ {-1, 0, 1}

class Pattern {
  final String? name;
  final String? url;
  final int? size;
  final String? type;          // 'corner' or null (translation-invariant)
  final List<SignedVertex> anchors;
  final List<SignedVertex> vertices;
}

class PatternMatch {
  final int symmetryIndex;     // 0..7 dihedral
  final bool invert;           // colours flipped
  final List<Vertex> anchors;
  final List<Vertex> vertices;
}

class BoardMatcher {
  static List<Pattern> get defaultLibrary;     // Sabaki, verbatim (58 patterns)
  static List<Pattern> get extendedLibrary;    // golo additions (3 patterns)
  static List<Pattern> get combinedLibrary;    // extended ++ default (default for nameMove)

  static String? nameMove(Board, Stone?, Vertex?, {library});
  static FoundPattern? findPatternInMove(Board, Stone?, Vertex?, {library});
  static Iterable<PatternMatch> matchShape(Board, Vertex anchor, Pattern);
  static Iterable<PatternMatch> matchCorner(Board, Pattern);
  static Iterable<FoundPattern> findAllPatterns(Board, {library});
}

extension BoardMatching on Board {
  String? nameMove(Stone?, Vertex?, {library});
  FoundPattern? findPatternInMove(Stone?, Vertex?, {library});
  Iterable<PatternMatch> matchShape(Vertex, Pattern);
  Iterable<PatternMatch> matchCorner(Pattern);
  Iterable<FoundPattern> findAllPatterns({library});
}

extension PatternLocalization on Pattern {
  String? localizedName(String locale);
}

class MoveLocalizations {
  factory MoveLocalizations.of(String locale);  // BCP-47 dashes + base-language fallback
  String translate(String canonicalName);
  String? translateOrNull(String? canonicalName);
  Iterable<String> get knownTerms;
  static const supportedLocales = ['en', 'ja', 'ko', 'zh', 'zh_HK', 'zh_TW'];
}
```

## Move classification

```dart
board.nameMove(Stone.black, (x: 3, y: 3));   // '4-4 Point'
board.nameMove(Stone.black, (x: 9, y: 9));   // 'Tengen'
board.nameMove(Stone.white, captureVertex);  // 'Take'
board.nameMove(Stone.black, atariVertex);    // 'Atari'
board.nameMove(Stone.black, badShape);       // 'Self-Atari'
board.nameMove(null, anyVertex);             // 'Pass'
```

Ordering: `Take` > `Atari` > `Suicide` > `Self-Atari` > `Fill` > `Connect` > library shape > `Tengen` / `Hoshi` / `<n>-<n> Point`.

`Self-Atari` is reported when the played stone (after captures) leaves its own chain at exactly 1 liberty. Capture takes precedence (capturing a stone that would otherwise leave you in atari is `Take`, not `Self-Atari`).

## Pattern matching

```dart
// Shape match anywhere on the board
final pattern = const Pattern(
  anchors: [(vertex: (x: 0, y: 2), sign: 1), (vertex: (x: 2, y: 2), sign: 1)],
  vertices: [
    (vertex: (x: 1, y: 1), sign: 1),
    (vertex: (x: 2, y: 1), sign: 0),
    (vertex: (x: 1, y: 2), sign: 0),
  ],
);
for (final m in board.matchShape((x: 14, y: 2), pattern)) {
  print('symmetry ${m.symmetryIndex}, vertices ${m.vertices}');
}

// Walk every library hit on the board
for (final fp in board.findAllPatterns()) {
  print('${fp.pattern.name}: ${fp.match.vertices}');
}
```

Each `PatternMatch` reports the dihedral `symmetryIndex` (0–7), `invert` (whether colours were flipped), and the matched on-board `anchors` and `vertices` lists.

## Curated opening library

`BoardMatcher.defaultLibrary` returns Sabaki's 58-pattern opening library (Chinese / High Chinese / Orthodox / Kobayashi / Shusaku / Micro Chinese / Sanrensei / Nirensei / common joseki / approaches / enclosures / point names / etc.). Embedded verbatim from upstream's `library/library.json`, parsed lazily and cached. Regenerate with `dart run tool/regen_board_matcher_library.dart`.

```dart
final lib = BoardMatcher.defaultLibrary;     // 58 patterns
print(lib.first.name);                        // 'Low Chinese Opening'
```

## Extended patterns (golo additions)

`BoardMatcher.extendedLibrary` adds three patterns and is placed **before** `defaultLibrary` in `combinedLibrary` so the more specific names win:

| Name | Senseis | Notes |
|------|---------|-------|
| `Crosscut` | [Crosscut](https://senseis.xmp.net/?Crosscut) | 2×2 alternating cut. Sabaki's `Cut` pattern depicts the same shape under a less-conventional name; we now report `Crosscut`. |
| `Monkey Jump` | [Monkey Jump](https://senseis.xmp.net/?MonkeyJump) | Corner-anchored 3-1 keima from 2nd line to 1st line on size 19. Anchors live one off the literal corner — `(18, 0)` would fold to `(0, 0)` under mod-based corner symmetry and become unmatchable. |
| `Cap` (boshi) | [Boshi](https://senseis.xmp.net/?Boshi) | One-space jump above an isolated opponent stone. Mid-board only — corner-anchored Approach patterns continue to win against 4-4 / 3-4 stones. |

## Localization

`MoveLocalizations` translates every move/pattern name into the same 6 locales `igo-social-flutter` ships:

```dart
MoveLocalizations.of('ja').translate('Atari');         // 'アタリ'
MoveLocalizations.of('ja').translate('4-4 Point');     // '星'
MoveLocalizations.of('ja').translate('Self-Atari');    // '自アタリ'
MoveLocalizations.of('zh-HK').translate('Suicide');    // '自殺'   (BCP-47 dashes work)
MoveLocalizations.of('zh_CN').translate('Atari');      // '打吃'   (base-language fallback)
MoveLocalizations.of('xx').translate('Atari');         // 'Atari'  (unknown → English)

pattern.localizedName('ja');                            // shortcut on Pattern
```

Source-of-truth ARB files at [`lib/l10n/`](lib/l10n/) (`app_en.arb`, `app_ja.arb`, `app_ko.arb`, `app_zh.arb`, `app_zh_HK.arb`, `app_zh_TW.arb`); runtime payload is embedded in `lib/src/move_localizations.dart`. An ARB ↔ Dart consistency test ([`test/move_localizations_test.dart`](test/move_localizations_test.dart)) makes drift impossible.

`zh_HK` and `zh_TW` currently share the same Traditional Chinese map; differentiate in `lib/src/move_localizations.dart` when you have specific regional forms in mind.

## Implementation notes

The matcher is a Dart-idiomatic rewrite, not a line-by-line port. Key choices:

- **Sign maps as flat `Int8List`** indexed `y * width + x` — no `Stone?` boxing, no nested-list indirection, cache-friendly.
- **Symmetry hypotheses as an 8-bit bitfield** instead of a `List<bool>` — one int per active hypothesis set.
- **Closed-form dihedral transforms** via `switch` — no per-call allocation of an 8-element record list.
- **Iterative chain liberty traversal** with `Int8List` visit/lib marks and capped early-exit (we only need to distinguish 1 / 2 / 3+).
- **Closure-free unrolled neighbour loops** in the hot paths.

Behavioural notes:
- `Self-Atari` is computed from the post-capture board state, so capturing-into-self-atari resolves as `Take`.
- `findPatternInMove` defaults to `combinedLibrary`; pass `library: defaultLibrary` to force Sabaki-only behaviour.
- Sabaki's `Cut` pattern → reported as `Crosscut` by default. Pass `library: defaultLibrary` to recover the original `Cut` label.

## Sensei's terms considered but not added

These need history or simulation, not a static shape:
- **Net (Geta)** — needs lookahead to confirm there's no escape.
- **Snapback** — two

